import Mathlib.Data.List.Basic

/-!
# A colourable trail that is not completable by simple operations (Kauffman, §4), certified

Data: a 3-connected planar cubic graph `G` on 20 vertices, the empty edge `e0 = (3, 8)`, a
proper 3-edge-colouring of `G`, the 36 trail colourings of `G - e0` (equal colours at each
endpoint), and for each trail colouring and colour pair the partition of the vertices into
two-colour components (each block listed in a search order, every vertex after the first
joined by an edge of the pair's colours to an earlier one), together with the index in the
list of the colouring obtained by switching that component.  The kernel verifies: the full
colouring is proper; each trail colouring is proper with equal endpoint colours; each
certified block is connected in the two-colour subgraph, the blocks partition the vertices,
every edge of the pair's colours stays inside a block (so the blocks are exactly the
components); the two endpoints of `e0` never share a block (so no completing pathway exists);
and switching any block gives a listed colouring (so the list is closed under simple
operations).  Hence the trail's formation is never completable by simple operations although
its extended graph is 3-edge-colourable.
-/

